Article 22 The banking regulatory authority of the State Council shall, within the prescribed time limits, make a written decision to approve or disapprove the following applications; if it decides to disapprove, it shall state the reasons:
(1) For the establishment of a banking financial institution, within six months from the date of receipt of the application documents;
(2) For the modification, termination, and the business scope or increase of business types within the business scope of a banking financial institution, within three months from the date of receipt of the application documents;
(3) For examining the qualifications of directors and senior officers, within thirty days from the date of receipt of the application documents.

Article 34 The banking regulatory authority may, based on the requirements of prudential supervision, take the following measures for on-site inspection:
(1) Entering a banking financial institution for inspection;
(2) Inquiring personnel of the banking financial institution and requiring them to provide explanations on the matters under inspection;
(3) Consulting and copying documents and materials of the banking financial institution related to the matters under inspection, and sealing up documents and materials that may be transferred, concealed, or destroyed;
(4) Inspecting the systems of the banking financial institution that use electronic computers to manage business data.
On-site inspection shall be subject to the approval of the person in charge of the banking regulatory authority. During on-site inspection, there shall be no fewer than two inspectors, and they shall present their lawful credentials and an inspection notice; if there are fewer than two inspectors or they fail to present their lawful credentials and inspection notice, the banking financial institution shall have the right to refuse the inspection.

Article 37 Where a banking financial institution violates the prudential operation rules, the banking regulatory authority of the State Council or its provincial-level office shall order it to make corrections within a specified time limit; if it fails to make corrections within the time limit, or if its conduct seriously jeopardizes the sound operation of the banking financial institution and harms the legitimate rights and interests of depositors and other customers, upon the approval of the person in charge of the banking regulatory authority of the State Council or its provincial-level office, the following measures may be taken according to the circumstances:
(1) Ordering the suspension of part of its business, or ceasing to approve the launch of new business;
(2) Restricting the distribution of dividends and other income;
(3) Restricting the transfer of assets;
(4) Ordering the controlling shareholder to transfer its equity, or restricting the rights of relevant shareholders;
(5) Ordering the adjustment of directors and senior officers, or restricting their rights;
(6) Ceasing to approve the establishment of additional branches.
After the banking financial institution has rectified the situation, it shall submit a report to the banking regulatory authority of the State Council or its provincial-level office. If, after verification, the banking regulatory authority of the State Council or its provincial-level office finds that the institution complies with the relevant prudential operation rules, it shall, within three days from the date of completion of the verification, lift the relevant measures taken against it under the preceding paragraph.

Article 42 When the banking regulatory authority conducts an inspection of a banking financial institution according to law, with the approval of the head of the banking regulatory authority at or above the level of a districted city, it may take the following measures against any unit or individual related to the suspected illegal matter:
(1) Inquiring of the relevant unit or individual and requesting explanations of the relevant circumstances;
(2) Inspecting and copying documents and materials such as financial accounting and property rights registration;
(3) Taking priority registration and preservation of documents and materials that may be transferred, concealed, destroyed, or forged.
When the banking regulatory authority takes the measures prescribed in the preceding paragraph, there shall be no less than two investigators, and they shall present their legal credentials and investigation notice; if there are fewer than two investigators or they fail to present legal credentials and investigation notice, the relevant unit or individual shall have the right to refuse. Units and individuals shall cooperate with the measures taken according to law, provide truthful explanations of the relevant circumstances, and supply relevant documents and materials, and shall not refuse, obstruct, or conceal.

Article 43 Where a staff member of the banking regulatory authority engaged in supervision and administration falls under any of the following circumstances, an administrative sanction shall be given according to law; if a crime is constituted, criminal liability shall be investigated according to law:
(1) Violating provisions in examining and approving the establishment, change, termination, business scope, and business types within the business scope of a banking financial institution;
(2) Violating provisions in conducting on-site inspections of banking financial institutions;
(3) Failing to report an emergency in accordance with Article 28 of this Law;
(4) Violating provisions in inquiring into accounts or applying for freezing of funds;
(5) Violating provisions in taking measures or imposing penalties against a banking financial institution;
(6) Violating the provisions of Article 42 of this Law in conducting investigations of relevant units or individuals;
(7) Other acts of abusing powers or neglecting duties.
If a staff member of the banking regulatory authority engaged in supervision and administration commits embezzlement or bribery, or divulges state secrets, trade secrets, or personal privacy, and a crime is constituted, criminal liability shall be investigated according to law; if no crime is constituted, an administrative sanction shall be given according to law.

Article 45 Where a banking financial institution falls under any of the following circumstances, the State Council's banking regulatory authority shall order rectification, and if there are illegal gains, confiscate the illegal gains; if the illegal gains are 500,000 yuan or more, a fine of not less than one time but not more than five times the illegal gains shall be imposed concurrently; if there are no illegal gains or the illegal gains are less than 500,000 yuan, a fine of not less than 500,000 yuan but not more than 2,000,000 yuan shall be imposed; if the circumstances are particularly serious or if rectification is not made within the time limit, it may order suspension of business for rectification or revoke its operating permit; if a crime is constituted, criminal liability shall be investigated according to law:
(1) Establishing branches without approval;
(2) Changing or terminating without approval;
(3) Engaging in business activities that are not approved or not recorded in violation of provisions;
(4) Raising or lowering deposit interest rates or loan interest rates in violation of provisions.

Article 46 Where a banking financial institution falls under any of the following circumstances, the State Council's banking regulatory authority shall order rectification and concurrently impose a fine of not less than 200,000 yuan but not more than 500,000 yuan; if the circumstances are particularly serious or if rectification is not made within the time limit, it may order suspension of business for rectification or revoke its operating permit; if a crime is constituted, criminal liability shall be investigated according to law:
(1) Appointing directors or senior officers without qualification review;
(2) Refusing or obstructing off-site supervision or on-site inspection;
(3) Providing false statements, reports, or other documents or materials that conceal important facts;
(4) Failing to conduct information disclosure in accordance with regulations;
(5) Seriously violating prudent operation rules;
(6) Refusing to implement the measures prescribed in Article 37 of this Law.

Article 48 Where a banking financial institution violates laws, administrative regulations, or the state's provisions on banking supervision and administration, the banking regulatory authority, in addition to imposing penalties in accordance with Articles 44 through 47 of this Law, may also, depending on the different circumstances, take the following measures:
(1) Ordering the banking financial institution to impose disciplinary sanctions on the directly responsible directors, senior officers, and other directly responsible persons;
(2) If the act of the banking financial institution does not constitute a crime, issuing a warning to the directly responsible directors, senior officers, and other directly responsible persons and imposing a fine of not less than 50,000 yuan but not more than 500,000 yuan;
(3) Disqualifying the directly responsible directors and senior officers from holding office for a specified period or for life, and prohibiting the directly responsible directors, senior officers, and other directly responsible persons from engaging in banking work for a specified period or for life.
